<LegalPage title="Cookie Policy" updated="October 27, 2026">
  <div class="legal__sec">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>This website is run by The Profectus Agency (“Profectus”, “we”, “us”), which has been in business since January 2023. This policy explains how we use cookies and similar technologies on this website, and the choices you have.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="legal__sec">
    <h2>What cookies are</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small text files that a website stores on your browser. When you visit our website, we store cookies on your browser to collect information. The information collected might relate to you, your preferences or your device, and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to and to provide a more personalized web experience.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="legal__sec">
    <h2>The cookies we use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Strictly Necessary.</b> These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. Some are only set in response to requests made by you, such as setting your preferences, logging in or filling out forms. They may also be set for certain security purposes and network management.</li>
      <li><b>Functional.</b> These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and improve your experience. They may be set by us or by third-party providers whose services have been added to our website.</li>
      <li><b>Performance.</b> These cookies allow us to engage in certain activities, such as counting visits and identifying traffic sources that assist us in measuring the performance of our website. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the website.</li>
      <li><b>Targeting.</b> These cookies are used to collect information about your browser, device and website visit and use such information to provide you with personalized experiences and advertising on this website and others across the internet.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Functional, Performance and Targeting cookies are on unless you switch them off. Today the site sets one cookie, <code>pf_consent</code>, which is strictly necessary: it remembers the choice you made in our cookie settings, for 12 months.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="legal__sec">
    <h2>How to manage cookies</h2>
    <p>You can change your choice at any time in our <button type="button" data-pfc-open aria-haspopup="dialog">Cookie Settings</button>, also linked at the bottom of every page. You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings, but it may affect your ability to use our website.</p>
    <p>If you are located in the United States, local law may provide you with the right to opt-out of the sale or sharing of your personal information to third parties. You can do this by switching off Targeting cookies in our Cookie Settings, or on our <a href="/do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</a> page.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="legal__sec">
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy when the cookies on our website change. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last updated.</p>
  </div>
</LegalPage>
